settings.description:
Thermostats expose the standard HA presets (Comfort / Eco / Sleep / Away / Vacation / Frost / Boost) per room. On the iPark Smarthome App option these also engage a software slow duty cycle (time-proportional control, not high-frequency PWM). Use the three importable HA Blueprints under `blueprints/automation/bestin/` for night setback / vacation / away schedules. See the [iPark Smarthome App guide](https://github.com/dlxmax/ha-bestin-fork/blob/main/guide/iparkapp.md#슬로우-듀티-사이클-제어--slow-duty-cycle-control) for details.

Room temperature sensors (optional, iPark Smarthome App only): through the app the wallpad's temperature arrives as whole degrees, rounded down, and the wall unit often reads high. Pick an HA temperature sensor for a room and its thermostat shows that sensor, and the duty cycle presets control on it. The wallpad's own reading stays available as the `wallpad_temperature` attribute. Leave a room empty to keep using the wallpad.
{rooms}
